1. legacy/android
   "Binaural Beats Therapy" by Giorgio Regni, an Android app published as the
   GitHub project GiorgioRegni/Binaural-Beats. License: GNU General Public
   License version 3, full text in legacy/android/LICENSE. The files in that
   folder are Giorgio Regni's work, not Zonked's, and stay under the GPLv3.

2. legacy/gnaural
   Three binaural beat schedules in the Gnaural XML format (Power Nap, a
   meditation schedule for airplane travel, and "Arrive sharp"). Each file
   names Gnaural as its source (see the gnaural.sourceforge.net link in the
   file header) and carries no license text of its own. They came with the
   GPLv3 Android app above. Treat them as third-party reference material.
   Gnaural itself is free software published under the GPL.

3. Templates derived from those sources
   21 templates in web/src/catalog/seeds.ts have source "android" and 3 have
   source "gnaural". They re-express published frequency and duration values
   only (beat Hz, step lengths, noise use). They copy no GPLv3 source code and
   no descriptive text. Template names and descriptions are original wording.
   A beat frequency or a duration is a number, not expression.

4. Lineage
   Zonked resurrects the 1998 SBaGen sequence idea and the author's 2018
   final-year web application, binaural beats research and yellow mask
   mascot. The 2018 work was created after studying Giorgio Regni's GPLv3
   Android app, which is credited here.

Zonked is not a medical device.
